! Quick Start Guide / 快速入门

Welcome to your Personal Knowledge Manager! This tool is built on [[TiddlyWiki|https://tiddlywiki.com]], customized for knowledge management.

!! Core Concepts

* ''Tiddler'' - The basic unit of content, like a note card. Each tiddler has a title, content, and optional tags.
* ''Tags'' - Organize tiddlers with tags. Click any tag to see related content.
* ''Links'' - Create links between tiddlers using `[[Title]]` syntax. The ''Freelinks'' plugin also auto-links tiddler titles.
* ''WikiText'' - TiddlyWiki's markup language. See [[WikiText Reference|https://tiddlywiki.com/#WikiText]] for details.

!! Key Features

|!Feature|!Description|
|Dashboard|Overview of your knowledge base with stats, recent items, and search|
|Journal|Daily journaling with date-stamped entries|
|Projects|Track projects with tasks and notes|
|Reading Notes|Book notes with status tracking (Reading/Done/ToRead)|
|Markdown|Write in Markdown (set tiddler type to `text/x-markdown`)|
|Math|LaTeX math with KaTeX: `$$E=mc^2$$`|
|Code Highlighting|Syntax highlighting for code blocks|
|Browser Storage|Auto-saves changes to browser local storage|
|Full Text Search|Built-in search across all content|
|Freelinks|Automatically links tiddler titles in text|

!! How to Save

This is a single HTML file. To save your changes:

# ''Browser Storage'' (automatic) - Changes are auto-saved to your browser's local storage
# ''Download'' - Click the save button (checkmark icon) in the sidebar to download the updated HTML file
# ''Replace'' the old file with the downloaded one to keep your data

!! Tips

* Use `Ctrl+Enter` to save a tiddler being edited
* Use `Escape` to cancel editing
* Click the `+` button or use the sidebar to create new tiddlers
* Use `[img[url]]` to embed images
* Use `<<tag "TagName">>` to create clickable tag pills
* Drag and drop files onto the wiki to import them
